---
# The playbooks are a delivered coursework artifact. Rewriting them to please a
# style checker would misrepresent what was handed in, so the rules they break
# are skipped here and named in "Known limitations" in the README instead.
#
# Nothing is skipped silently: every entry below says what the code does wrong.

profile: basic

skip_list:
  # --- cosmetic ---
  # Short module names (user, service, copy) instead of ansible.builtin.user.
  - fqcn
  # `yes` instead of `true`. Both are valid YAML booleans.
  - yaml[truthy]
  # Trailing blank line at the end of a file.
  - yaml[empty-lines]

  # --- real defects, documented in the README ---
  # configurar_web.yml stops the other web server with ignore_errors instead of
  # a failed_when condition, so it would also swallow an unrelated failure.
  - ignore-errors
  # The two `copy` tasks that write index.html do not set a mode, so the file
  # lands with whatever umask the remote has.
  - risky-file-permissions
  # One task name puts "{{ web_service }}" in the middle instead of at the end,
  # which makes the log line harder to group.
  - name[template]
